          "modifiedDate": "2026-02-03T14:53:35Z",
          "name": "52-working-with-sections",
          "sectionId": "3B0B704C-A12C-4AF7-B81F-8E8E0134AB98",
          "userOrder": 1,
          "versions": [
            {
              "comments": [],
              "content": "# Working with Sections\n\nSections help you organize files in Prose projects into logical groups. This guide covers creating, managing, and using sections effectively.\n\n## Understanding Sections\n\nSections are organizational containers within a Prose project:\n- Each section can hold multiple files\n- Files can be assigned to one section (or none)\n- Sections appear in the main file list as collapsible groups\n\n### Examples of Section Use\n- **User Guide**: \"Introduction\", \"Features\", \"Reference\", \"Appendix\"\n- **Essay Collection**: \"Personal\", \"Academic\", \"Published\"\n- **Blog Archive**: \"2024\", \"2025\", \"Drafts\"\n- **Research Project**: \"Literature Review\", \"Methods\", \"Results\", \"Discussion\"\n\n## Creating Sections\n\n### From the Sections Folder\n1. Navigate to your Prose project\n2. Tap the **Sections** folder\n3. Tap **+** (or Add Section)\n4. Enter a section name\n5. Optionally add a synopsis\n6. Tap **Create**\n\n### Section Properties\n- **Name**: The section title (required)\n- **Synopsis**: Brief description (optional)\n- **Order**: Sections can be reordered by dragging\n\n## Managing Sections\n\n### Viewing Sections\nOpen the **Sections** folder to see all sections with:\n- Section name\n- File count\n- Synopsis preview\n\n### Reordering Sections\n1. In the Sections folder, tap **Edit**\n2. Drag sections using the grip handle\n3. Tap **Done**\n\nThe order affects how sections appear in the main file list.\n\n### Renaming a Section\n1. Tap the section row's menu (⋯)\n2. Select **Rename**\n3. Enter the new name\n4. Tap **Save**\n\n### Deleting a Section\n1. Tap the section row's menu (⋯)\n2. Select **Delete**\n3. Confirm deletion\n\n**Note**: Deleting a section unassigns its files (moves them to \"Unassigned\") but does not delete the files themselves.\n\n## Assigning Files to Sections\n\n### From the Main File List\n1. In the Prose folder, tap **Edit**\n2. Select one or more files (must have **Ready** status)\n3. Tap **Add to Section** in the bottom toolbar\n4. Choose the destination section\n5. Files are moved to that section\n\n### Why Ready Status Required?\nOnly files marked as \"Ready\" can be assigned to sections. This encourages completing drafts before organizing them into the final structure.\n\n### Changing a File's Section\nTo move a file to a different section:\n1. Select the file in Edit mode\n2. Tap **Add to Section**\n3. Choose the new section\n\n### Removing from a Section\nTo unassign a file from its section:\n1. Select the file in Edit mode\n2. Tap **Add to Section**\n3. Choose **None** or **Unassigned**\n\n## The Collapsible Section View\n\nWhen files are assigned to sections, the main file list displays them grouped:\n\n### Section Headers\nEach section shows:\n- Disclosure triangle (▶/▼)\n- Folder icon\n- Section name\n- File count in parentheses\n\n### Expanding and Collapsing\n- **Tap a section header** to expand or collapse it\n- **Expand/Collapse All**: Use the toolbar button to toggle all sections\n\n### Unassigned Section\nFiles not assigned to any section appear in an \"Unassigned\" group at the bottom of the list.\n\n### When Sections Appear\nThe collapsible section view only appears when:\n- Multiple sections exist with assigned files\n- You're viewing the main Prose file list (not a specific section)\n\n## Viewing Section Contents\n\n### From the Main List\nExpand a section header to see its files inline.\n\n### From the Sections Folder\n1. Open the **Sections** folder\n2. Tap a section name\n3. View only that section's files\n\nThis dedicated view allows:\n- Reordering files within the section\n- Focused editing without other sections visible\n\n## Reordering Files Within a Section\n\nWhen viewing a specific section's files:\n1. Drag files to reorder them\n2. Order is preserved for export\n\nThe order matters for:\n- Export order when generating combined documents\n- Reading sequence\n\n## Tips for Using Sections\n\n### Plan Your Structure\nBefore creating sections, sketch out your project's organization. It's easier to assign files to a planned structure than to reorganize later.\n\n### Use Descriptive Names\nSection names should clearly indicate content: \"Chapter 1: Introduction\" rather than just \"Chapter 1\".\n\n### Keep Sections Manageable\nIf a section has 20+ files, consider splitting it into subsections or rethinking your organization.\n\n### Review Unassigned Files\nPeriodically check the Unassigned group—these files may need to be organized or deleted.\n\n### Export by Section\nWhen exporting, you can choose to export individual sections as separate documents.\n\n## See Also\n- [Prose Mode Overview](01-prose-mode-overview.md)\n- [File Organization](03-file-organization.md)\n- [Folders and Files](../03-projects/04-folders-and-files.md)\n\n---\n",
              "createdDate": "2026-02-03T14:52:32Z",
              "footnotes": [],
              "id": "642AEF7B-C60F-4FC8-9716-03DE90EE570D",
              "versionNumber": 1
            }
