              "comments": [],
              "content": "# Quick Start Guide\n\nGet writing in Writing Shed Pro in just five minutes. This guide walks you through creating your first project and writing your first document.\n\n## Step 1: Create a Project\n\nWhen you first open Writing Shed Pro, you'll see an empty project list.\n\n1. Tap the **+** button in the toolbar\n2. Enter a name for your project (e.g., \"My First Project\")\n3. Choose a project type:\n   - **Prose** for general writing\n   - **Poetry** for poems and verse\n   - **Fiction** for stories and novels\n   - **Drama** for scripts and plays\n4. Tap **Create**\n\nYour new project appears in the list. Tap it to open.\n\n## Step 2: Understand the Folder Structure\n\nEvery project starts with a standard folder structure:\n\n- **Draft** – Works in progress\n- **Ready** – Completed pieces\n- **Set Aside** – Items you're not currently working on\n- **Trash** – Deleted items (can be restored)\n\nPoetry and short fiction projects also include:\n- **Collections** – Groups of files for organization\n- **Publications** – Magazines and competitions you submit to\n- **Submissions** – Track what you've sent where\n\n## Step 3: Create Your First File\n\n1. Tap the **Draft** folder to open it\n2. Tap the **+** button\n3. Enter a title for your file\n4. Tap **Create**\n\nThe file opens automatically in the editor.\n\n## Step 4: Write!\n\nStart typing. The editor works like any word processor:\n\n- Type naturally with the on-screen keyboard (iOS) or physical keyboard (Mac)\n- Text auto-saves as you type\n- Use the formatting toolbar above the keyboard for styling\n\n### Basic Formatting\n\nThe formatting toolbar provides quick access to:\n\n- **¶** – Change paragraph style (Body, Heading, etc.)\n- **B** – Bold\n- *I* – Italic\n- **U** – Underline\n- **S̶** – Strikethrough\n- **⊕** – Insert menu (images, footnotes, comments)\n\n## Step 5: Save Your Work\n\nWriting Shed Pro auto-saves continuously. Every change is preserved automatically:\n\n- Changes sync to iCloud within seconds\n- Your work is always backed up\n- No \"Save\" button needed\n\nTo see your save history, look at file versions in the file details view.\n\n## Step 6: Organize Your Work\n\nAs you write more, keep things organized:\n\n### Move Files Between Folders\n1. Long-press a file\n2. Choose **Move to...**\n3. Select the destination folder\n\n### Create Subfolders\n1. In any folder, tap **+**\n2. Choose **New Folder**\n3. Enter a name\n\n### Reorder Files\n1. Tap **Edit** in the file list\n2. Drag files using the handle on the right\n3. Tap **Done**\n\n## What's Next?\n\nYou've learned the basics! Here's where to go next:\n\n- **[The Interface Tour](../02-getting-started/03-the-interface-tour.md)** – Explore all the views and controls\n- **[Text Formatting](../04-writing/02-text-formatting.md)** – Master styles and formatting\n- **[Poetry Mode Overview](../06-poetry-features/01-poetry-mode-overview.md)** – If you're a poet\n- **[Fiction Mode Overview](../07-fiction-features/01-fiction-mode-overview.md)** – If you're writing fiction\n\n## Tips for New Users\n\n1. **Use iCloud** – Enable iCloud sync in Settings for seamless multi-device access\n2. **Explore project types** – Each type has specialized features worth trying\n3. **Learn the keyboard shortcuts** – They'll speed up your workflow significantly\n4. **Check the reference section** – Quick answers when you need them\n\n## See Also\n- [Introduction](01-introduction.md)\n- [Creating Your First Project](../02-getting-started/02-creating-your-first-project.md)\n- [The Editor](../04-writing/01-the-editor.md)\n\n---\n",
