          "id": "634E1F4F-14C5-4854-B604-1C5AA97BECD7",
          "includedInManuscript": true,
          "modifiedDate": "2026-02-03T15:35:27Z",
          "name": "107-contributors",
          "sectionId": "1A4A60D7-55FE-49AF-9636-75122540D6B9",
          "userOrder": 6,
          "versions": [
            {
              "comments": [],
              "content": "# Contributors\n\nThe Contributors section is a back matter feature designed for magazine editors, anthology publishers, and anyone who needs to list the contributors to a publication with their biographical notes.\n\n## Overview\n\nContributors is a user-created list (unlike auto-generated back matter like Endnotes or Glossary). Each entry contains:\n\n- **First Name** — The contributor's given name\n- **Surname** — The contributor's family/last name  \n- **Biography** — A biographical note about the contributor\n\nThe list is automatically sorted alphabetically by surname, then by first name.\n\n## Setting Up Contributors\n\n### Enable the Contributors File\n\n1. Open your project\n2. Navigate to **Manuscript → Back Matter**\n3. Open **Back Matter Settings** from the folder menu\n4. Enable **Contributors**\n5. A \"Contributors\" file will be created in the Back Matter folder\n\n### Adding a Contributor\n\n1. Open the **Contributors** file in Back Matter\n2. Tap the **+** button in the toolbar\n3. Fill in the contributor details:\n   - **First Name**: Enter the contributor's first name\n   - **Surname**: Enter the contributor's surname/last name\n   - **Biography**: Write a biographical note (can be multiple paragraphs)\n4. Tap **Save**\n\nThe new contributor appears in the list, automatically sorted by surname.\n\n### Editing a Contributor\n\n1. Tap on the contributor entry you want to edit\n2. The editor sheet opens with the existing details\n3. Make your changes\n4. Tap **Save**\n\n### Deleting a Contributor\n\nYou can delete contributors in two ways:\n\n**Swipe to Delete:**\n1. Swipe left on the contributor entry\n2. Tap the **Delete** button\n\n**Context Menu:**\n1. Long-press on the contributor entry\n2. Select **Delete** from the context menu\n3. Confirm the deletion\n\n## Export Format\n\nWhen you export your manuscript to PDF or print, the Contributors section appears in the back matter with this format:\n\n```\nCONTRIBUTORS\n\nJones, Sarah\nSarah Jones is a poet whose work has appeared in numerous\nliterary magazines. She lives in Portland, Oregon.\n\nSmith, John\nJohn Smith is the author of three novels and has won\nthe National Book Award for Fiction.\n```\n\nContributors are sorted alphabetically by surname in the exported document.\n\n## Tips\n\n### Writing Effective Biographies\n\n- Keep biographies concise (2-4 sentences is typical)\n- Include relevant credentials or publications\n- Mention the contributor's location if appropriate\n- Use third person (\"Sarah Jones is...\" not \"I am...\")\n\n### Managing Many Contributors\n\nFor anthologies with many contributors:\n- Add contributors as you accept submissions\n- Use consistent formatting for all biographies\n- Review the full list before export to ensure alphabetical ordering looks correct\n\n## Related Topics\n\n- [Back Matter Overview](../7-fiction-features/74-manuscript-formatting.md)\n- [PDF Export](../9-publishing/92-pdf-export.md)\n- [Manuscript Assembly](../7-fiction-features/74-manuscript-formatting.md)\n",
              "createdDate": "2026-02-03T15:34:54Z",
              "footnotes": [],
              "id": "3269456C-3F1A-4729-824E-C53DEA9BE930",
              "versionNumber": 1
            }
          ],
          "workflowStatus": "ready"
