          "name": "45-footnotes",
          "sectionId": "B95EE76A-A19C-4C3A-89E6-50DFD1A973AC",
          "userOrder": 4,
          "versions": [
            {
              "comments": [],
              "content": "# Footnotes\n\nFootnotes let you add supplementary information without interrupting the flow of your text. They're essential for academic writing, useful for annotations, and can add depth to fiction and poetry.\n\n## Understanding Footnotes\n\nA footnote consists of two parts:\n1. **Marker**: A superscript number in your text (¹, ², ³)\n2. **Content**: The actual note text, displayed at the page bottom\n\nWriting Shed Pro numbers footnotes automatically.\n\n## Inserting a Footnote\n\n1. Place cursor where you want the footnote marker\n2. Tap the **⊕** (Insert) button in the toolbar\n3. Select **Footnote**\n4. Type your footnote text in the editor that appears\n5. Tap **Save** or **Done**\n\nThe marker appears in your text as a superscript number.\n\n## Editing a Footnote\n\n### Quick Edit\n1. Tap the footnote marker in your text\n2. The footnote editor opens\n3. Make your changes\n4. Tap **Save**\n\n### From Footnotes List\n1. Access **Footnotes...** from the menu\n2. Find the footnote you want to edit\n3. Tap to edit\n4. Save your changes\n\n## Viewing All Footnotes\n\nTo see all footnotes in your document:\n\n1. Open the file menu\n2. Select **Footnotes...**\n\nThe list shows:\n- Footnote number\n- Preview of content\n- Location in document\n\nTap any footnote to jump to its marker in the text.\n\n## Deleting a Footnote\n\n### From the Text\n1. Select the footnote marker\n2. Press Delete/Backspace\n\n### From the Footnotes List\n1. Open **Footnotes...**\n2. Swipe left on the footnote\n3. Tap **Delete**\n4. Confirm\n\nWhen you delete a footnote, remaining footnotes renumber automatically.\n\n## Automatic Numbering\n\nFootnotes are numbered sequentially:\n- First footnote is ¹\n- Second is ²\n- And so on...\n\n### Renumbering\nWhen you add or delete footnotes:\n- All numbers update automatically\n- References stay accurate\n- No manual renumbering needed\n\n## Footnotes vs Endnotes\n\nWriting Shed Pro supports two display modes:\n\n### Footnotes Mode\n- Notes appear at the bottom of the page where referenced\n- Traditional academic and book style\n- Better for frequent reference\n\n### Endnotes Mode\n- All notes appear at the end of the document\n- Cleaner page layout\n- Common in some publication styles\n\n### Switching Modes\n1. Open document settings\n2. Find **Footnote Display**\n3. Choose **Footnotes** or **Endnotes**\n\nThe content doesn't change—only where it appears.\n\n## Footnotes in Pagination View\n\nIn pagination view (full-page layout):\n- Footnotes appear at page bottom\n- A separator line divides text from footnotes\n- Long footnotes may continue on the next page\n- Professional typesetting rules apply\n\n### Pagination Rules\n- Minimum 2 lines of body text above footnotes\n- Long footnotes split with continuation\n- Proper spacing maintained\n\n## Footnote Formatting\n\nFootnote text uses the **Footnote** paragraph style:\n- Typically smaller than body text\n- May have different indentation\n- Customize in Stylesheet Editor\n\n### Customizing Footnote Style\n1. Open Stylesheet Editor\n2. Find the Footnote style\n3. Adjust font, size, spacing as needed\n4. Save\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Keep Notes Concise\nFootnotes should supplement, not replace, main text. If a note is very long, consider incorporating the information elsewhere.\n\n### Number Placement\nPlace footnote markers:\n- After punctuation when possible\n- At natural pause points\n- Consistently throughout\n\n### Use Appropriately\n- Academic: Citations, clarifications\n- Fiction: Historical context, translations\n- Poetry: References, variations\n\n### Review Before Export\nCheck footnotes in pagination view before exporting to ensure they appear correctly.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Footnotes Not Showing in Export\n- Ensure export format supports footnotes\n- Check pagination view first\n- PDF and RTF support footnotes\n\n### Wrong Numbers\n- Delete and re-add if persistent\n- Check for duplicate markers\n- Renumbering is automatic\n\n### Marker Hard to See\n- Markers are styled as small superscripts\n- Zoom in if needed\n- They're tappable despite small size\n\n## See Also\n- [The Editor](01-the-editor.md)\n- [Pagination](../07-publishing/05-pagination.md)\n- [PDF Export](../07-publishing/02-pdf-export.md)\n\n---\n",
