          "userOrder": 5,
          "versions": [
            {
              "comments": [],
              "content": "# Comments\n\nComments let you add notes, feedback, and reminders without modifying your text. They're perfect for revision notes, editor feedback, and collaborative review.\n\n## Understanding Comments\n\nComments appear as small indicators in your text:\n- A speech bubble icon marks the comment location\n- Tap to reveal the full comment content\n- Comments don't print or export (by default)\n\n## Adding a Comment\n\n1. Place cursor where you want the comment\n2. Tap the **⊕** (Insert) button in the toolbar\n3. Select **Comment**\n4. Type your comment text\n5. Tap **Save**\n\nA comment indicator appears at that position.\n\n## Viewing Comments\n\n### Tap to View\nTap any comment indicator to see:\n- The comment text\n- When it was created\n- Options to edit or delete\n\n### Comments Panel\nFor documents with many comments:\n1. Open the view menu\n2. Select **Comments**\n3. See all comments in a list\n\n## Editing Comments\n\n1. Tap the comment indicator\n2. The comment popover appears\n3. Tap to edit the text\n4. Save your changes\n\n## Deleting Comments\n\n### From the Document\n1. Tap the comment indicator\n2. In the popover, tap **Delete**\n3. Confirm if prompted\n\n### From Comments Panel\n1. Open the Comments panel\n2. Swipe left on the comment\n3. Tap **Delete**\n\n## Resolving Comments\n\nWhen you've addressed a comment:\n1. Tap the comment indicator\n2. Tap **Resolve**\n\nResolved comments:\n- Appear grayed out\n- Remain in the document\n- Can be filtered in the Comments panel\n- Can be \"unresolve\" if needed\n\n## Comment Workflow\n\n### For Self-Review\nUse comments to mark:\n- Sections needing revision\n- Research to add later\n- Questions to consider\n- Alternative phrasings\n\n### For Feedback\nShare documents with editors or beta readers who can:\n- Add their comments\n- Suggest changes\n- Ask questions\n\n### For Revision\nWork through comments systematically:\n1. Open Comments panel\n2. Address each comment\n3. Resolve when done\n4. Delete or keep for reference\n\n## Comments vs Footnotes\n\n| Feature | Comments | Footnotes |\n|---------|----------|-----------|\n| Visible in export | No (by default) | Yes |\n| For readers | No | Yes |\n| Numbered | No | Yes |\n| Purpose | Notes to self/collaborators | Reader information |\n\nUse footnotes for reader-facing notes; use comments for behind-the-scenes notes.\n\n## Comment Best Practices\n\n### Be Specific\n- Reference the exact issue\n- Explain what needs attention\n- Suggest solutions when possible\n\n### Stay Organized\n- Resolve comments as you address them\n- Delete unnecessary comments\n- Review before final export\n\n### Use Consistently\n- Develop a personal comment system\n- Example: [TODO], [CHECK], [REVISE]\n- Makes filtering easier\n\n## Comments in Different Contexts\n\n### Poetry\n- Note potential word alternatives\n- Mark rhythm problems\n- Track revision history\n\n### Fiction\n- Scene notes\n- Character consistency checks\n- Plot hole reminders\n\n### Academic\n- Citation reminders\n- Fact-check notes\n- Argument strengthening\n\n## Platform Differences\n\n### iOS\n- Comment popover from bottom\n- Full-screen on iPhone\n- Popover on iPad\n\n### Mac\n- Comment popover anchored to indicator\n- Click outside to dismiss\n- Keyboard navigation supported\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Comment Not Visible\n- Zoom in to see small indicators\n- Check if comments are filtered\n- Ensure comment was saved\n\n### Too Many Comments\n- Use Resolve to hide addressed ones\n- Filter in Comments panel\n- Delete unnecessary comments\n\n### Comments in Export\n- By default, comments don't export\n- Check export settings if you want them included\n- Consider converting to footnotes if readers should see them\n\n## See Also\n- [The Editor](01-the-editor.md)\n- [Footnotes](05-footnotes.md)\n- [Organizing Your Work](../03-projects/05-organizing-your-work.md)\n\n---\n",
              "createdDate": "2026-02-03T14:50:12Z",
