            {
              "comments": [],
              "content": "# Frequently Asked Questions\n\nCommon questions about Writing Shed Pro.\n\n## General\n\n### What is Writing Shed Pro?\nWriting Shed Pro is a professional writing app for creative writers. It supports prose, poetry, fiction, and drama with specialized tools for each.\n\n### What devices does it run on?\n- iPhone running iOS 17 or later\n- iPad running iPadOS 17 or later\n- Mac running macOS 14 (Sonoma) or later\n\n### Do my files sync between devices?\nYes. With iCloud enabled, your projects sync automatically across all your Apple devices.\n\n### Is my data backed up?\niCloud provides automatic backup. For extra safety, you can export important work as PDF or RTF.\n\n### Can I use it offline?\nYes. You can write offline. Changes sync when you reconnect.\n\n## Projects\n\n### What's the difference between project types?\n- **Prose**: General writing with no specialized tools\n- **Poetry**: Syllable counting, rhyme detection, verse tools\n- **Fiction**: Chapters, scenes, plot tracking\n- **Drama**: Script formatting with DML\n\n### Can I change a project's type?\nNo. Project type is set at creation. You can copy content to a new project of a different type.\n\n### What are Draft, Ready, and Trash?\n- **Draft**: Work in progress\n- **Ready**: Finished work\n- **Trash**: Deleted files (can be recovered)\n\n### How do I share a project?\nExport your project or individual files as PDF or RTF, then share using the standard share sheet.\n\n## Writing\n\n### Does it have spell check?\nYes. The system spell checker is active while you write.\n\n### Is there a word count goal?\nWord count is displayed but there's no built-in goal tracking.\n\n### How do I add images?\nIn the editor, use Insert → Image. You can add from Photos, Files, or Camera.\n\n### Are footnotes supported?\nYes. Insert footnotes through the Format menu or toolbar. They appear at page bottom.\n\n## Poetry\n\n### How accurate is the syllable counter?\nVery accurate for standard English. Some proper nouns and unusual words may need manual counting.\n\n### What's the CMU dictionary?\nThe Carnegie Mellon Pronouncing Dictionary provides pronunciation data for syllable counting and rhyme detection.\n\n### Can I create my own poetry forms?\nYou can select from built-in forms. Custom form creation may be added in future updates.\n\n## Fiction\n\n### How do chapters and scenes work?\nScenes are individual files. Chapters are folders that contain scenes. You control the structure.\n\n### What are plot elements?\nPlot elements (Setups, Conflicts, Resolutions) help you track story structure. Scenes can link to plot elements.\n\n### Is there character management?\nBasic character notes are supported. Full character management may be added in future updates.\n\n## Drama\n\n### What is DML?\nDrama Markup Language—a simple way to write scripts using plain text that formats automatically.\n\n### Can I export to Final Draft?\nCurrently, exports are PDF and RTF. Industry-specific formats may be added later.\n\n### Film or stage—which should I choose?\nChoose based on your target production. You can preview both formats from the same DML source.\n\n## Export and Printing\n\n### What formats can I export?\n- PDF (recommended for most uses)\n- RTF (Rich Text Format)\n\n### Can I export to Word (.docx)?\nRTF exports can be opened in Word. Direct .docx export may be added later.\n\n### How do I print?\nUse the standard Print option. Works on Mac and iPad with compatible printers.\n\n## Sync and Storage\n\n### How much iCloud storage do I need?\nDepends on your usage. Text uses minimal storage. Images use more. Most users need less than 1GB.\n\n### Can I use it without iCloud?\nYes, but sync between devices won't work. Your data stays on the device.\n\n### I have a new device—where's my data?\nSign into iCloud with the same Apple ID. Install Writing Shed Pro. Your projects will appear.\n\n### Why is sync slow?\nFirst sync may take time. Large projects take longer. Poor internet slows sync. Wait and check again.\n\n## Technical\n\n### Can I access files in the Files app?\nWriting Shed Pro uses its own storage. Export files if you need them in Files.\n\n### Does it work with external keyboards?\nYes. Full keyboard shortcut support on iPad and Mac.\n\n### Is there a web version?\nNo. Writing Shed Pro is a native Apple app only.\n\n### Can I use it on Windows or Android?\nNo. It's exclusive to Apple platforms.\n\n## Subscription and Purchase\n\n### Is there a free trial?\nCheck the App Store for current trial offerings.\n\n### Is it a subscription or one-time purchase?\nCheck the App Store for current pricing model.\n\n### Can I get a refund?\nContact Apple for App Store refunds.\n\n## Support\n\n### How do I report a bug?\nContact support with detailed steps to reproduce the issue.\n\n### Where do I request features?\nSubmit feature requests through the support channel.\n\n### Is there a community forum?\nCheck the app's website for community resources.\n\n## Future Development\n\n### Will [feature] be added?\nPopular feature requests are considered for future updates. Submit yours through support.\n\n### How often is the app updated?\nRegular updates address bugs and add features. Update notifications come through the App Store.\n\n### Can I beta test new versions?\nBeta testing opportunities may be announced through the app's website or newsletter.\n\n## See Also\n- [Troubleshooting](03-troubleshooting.md)\n- [Contact Support](05-contact-support.md)\n- [What's New](../01-welcome/02-whats-new.md)\n\n---\n",
              "createdDate": "2026-02-04T09:22:01Z",
