          "name": "93-rtf-export",
          "sectionId": "95D841AA-7A8E-4DD8-99EE-874424C3609A",
          "userOrder": 2,
          "versions": [
            {
              "comments": [],
              "content": "# RTF Export\n\nRTF (Rich Text Format) produces editable documents compatible with most word processors. Use RTF when you need recipients to be able to edit the content.\n\n## Why RTF?\n\n### Advantages\n- **Editable**: Recipients can make changes\n- **Compatible**: Opens in Word, Pages, Google Docs, etc.\n- **Standard**: Long-established format\n- **Lightweight**: Smaller than some alternatives\n\n### When to Use RTF\n- Sending to editors who need to make changes\n- Collaboration requiring editing\n- Importing into other applications\n- When PDF isn't accepted\n\n## Exporting to RTF\n\n### Single File\n1. Open the file\n2. Tap the **Share** or **Export** button\n3. Select **Export as RTF**\n4. Choose where to save or how to share\n\n### Multiple Files\n1. Open the collection, submission, or project\n2. Select files to export\n3. Choose **RTF**\n4. Files export (possibly as separate files or combined)\n\n## What's Preserved in RTF\n\n### Fully Preserved\n- Text content\n- Bold, italic, underline, strikethrough\n- Font family and size\n- Paragraph alignment\n- Line spacing\n- Basic colors\n\n### Usually Preserved\n- Images (may resize)\n- Footnotes (may format differently)\n- Paragraph spacing\n- Indentation\n\n### May Vary\n- Complex styles\n- Advanced typography\n- Exact pagination\n- Headers/footers\n\n## RTF Limitations\n\nRTF is an interchange format, not a final format:\n\n### Appearance May Differ\n- Different apps render RTF differently\n- Pagination won't match exactly\n- Fonts may substitute if unavailable\n\n### Feature Differences\n- Some formatting options don't translate\n- Complex layouts may simplify\n- App-specific features are lost\n\n### It's a Starting Point\nRecipients may need to:\n- Adjust formatting\n- Set up page layout\n- Apply their own styles\n\n## Working with Recipients\n\n### Communicate Expectations\n- Let editors know it's RTF\n- Mention if specific formatting matters\n- Be flexible about final appearance\n\n### Provide Context\n- Include any special instructions\n- Note if fonts need to be installed\n- Explain any unusual formatting\n\n### Accept Changes\nRTF is for editing. The document will likely change.\n\n## RTF vs PDF\n\n| Aspect | RTF | PDF |\n|--------|-----|-----|\n| Editable | Yes | No |\n| Appearance | Varies | Fixed |\n| File size | Smaller | Larger |\n| Features | Some lost | All preserved |\n| Use case | Collaboration | Final output |\n\n### Choose RTF When:\n- Editors need to make changes\n- Importing to another tool\n- File size is critical\n- PDF isn't an option\n\n### Choose PDF When:\n- Appearance must be exact\n- Submitting final work\n- Protecting content\n- Professional presentation\n\n## Troubleshooting RTF\n\n### Formatting Looks Wrong\n- Different apps interpret RTF differently\n- Try opening in a different app\n- Accept that some variation is normal\n\n### Images Missing\n- RTF image support varies\n- Check export settings\n- Try re-inserting images\n\n### File Won't Open\n- Check the app supports RTF\n- Try a different RTF viewer\n- File may be corrupted—re-export\n\n### Fonts Don't Match\n- Fonts must be installed on recipient's device\n- RTF substitutes if fonts are missing\n- Consider using common fonts (Times, Arial)\n\n## Alternatives to RTF\n\nIf RTF doesn't meet your needs:\n\n### DOCX\n- Better Word compatibility\n- More features preserved\n- Larger files\n- (May be available in future updates)\n\n### Plain Text\n- Maximum compatibility\n- No formatting\n- Smallest files\n\n### PDF\n- For final output\n- Not editable\n- Exact appearance\n\n## See Also\n- [Export Options](01-export-options.md)\n- [PDF Export](02-pdf-export.md)\n- [Printing](04-printing.md)\n\n---\n",
              "createdDate": "2026-02-03T15:13:54Z",
