          "userOrder": 2,
          "versions": [
            {
              "comments": [],
              "content": "# The Interface Tour\n\nThis guide walks you through Writing Shed Pro's interface, helping you understand where everything is and how to navigate efficiently.\n\n## Main Screen: Project List\n\nWhen you launch Writing Shed Pro, you see the **Project List**. This is your home base.\n\n### Project List Elements\n- **Navigation Bar**: Shows \"Projects\" title and action buttons\n- **Add Button (+)**: Create new projects\n- **Sort Button**: Change project ordering\n- **Project Cards**: Each project shows its name, type, and last modified date\n\n### Project Actions\n- **Tap** a project to open it\n- **Swipe left** to delete\n- **Long-press** for more options (rename, duplicate, details)\n\n## Inside a Project\n\nTapping a project opens its folder structure. The layout adapts to your device:\n\n### iPhone Layout\n- **Single-column navigation**: Tap folders to drill down\n- **Back button**: Return to previous level\n- **Long-press back button**: Jump directly to the project root\n\n### iPad and Mac Layout\n- **Sidebar**: Shows folder hierarchy\n- **Content area**: Shows selected folder's contents or file editor\n- **Optional inspector**: Shows details about selected items\n\n## The Toolbar\n\nThe toolbar appears at the top of most screens and provides context-specific actions.\n\n### Project View Toolbar\n- **Back arrow**: Return to project list\n- **Project name**: Tap to edit\n- **Gear icon**: Project settings\n- **Question mark**: Open user guide\n\n### Folder View Toolbar\n- **Back arrow**: Return to parent folder\n- **Folder name**: Current location\n- **Add (+)**: Create files or subfolders\n- **Edit**: Enter edit mode for reordering and deletion\n- **Sort**: Change sort order\n\n### File Editor Toolbar\n- **Back arrow**: Return to folder\n- **File name**: Tap to rename\n- **Formatting toolbar**: Text styling options\n- **More (...)**: Additional actions\n\n## The Formatting Toolbar\n\nWhen editing text, a formatting toolbar appears above the keyboard:\n\n| Button | Function |\n|--------|----------|\n| **¶** | Paragraph style picker (Body, Heading 1-3, etc.) |\n| **B** | Bold |\n| *I* | Italic |\n| **U** | Underline |\n| **S̶** | Strikethrough |\n| **⊕** | Insert menu (images, footnotes, comments) |\n\n### Paragraph Style Picker\nTap **¶** to see available paragraph styles:\n- Body (default text)\n- Heading 1, 2, 3\n- Subheadline\n- Caption\n- Footnote\n- And more...\n\nTap a style to apply it to the current paragraph.\n\n### Insert Menu\nTap **⊕** to insert:\n- **Image**: Add a photo or illustration\n- **Footnote**: Create a numbered footnote\n- **Comment**: Add a revision note\n\n## The Text Selection Menu\n\nWhen you select text by double-tapping or dragging, a menu appears:\n\n- **Cut**: Remove and copy to clipboard\n- **Copy**: Copy to clipboard\n- **Paste**: Insert from clipboard\n- **Select All**: Select entire document\n- **Look Up**: Dictionary and web search\n- **Translate**: Apple's translation\n- **Edit Style**: Open the style editor\n\n## Specialized Views\n\n### Poetry Projects\n- **Form Reference Panel**: Shows the rules for your selected poetry form\n- **Metrics Display**: Syllable counts and stress patterns per line\n\n### Fiction Projects\n- **Plot Outline**: Visual timeline of plot elements\n- **Scene Detail**: Edit scene content and metadata\n- **Character/Location Lists**: Manage story elements\n\n### Drama Projects\n- **DML Editor**: Write scripts in Drama Markup Language\n- **Preview Mode**: See formatted output (film or stage format)\n\n## Navigation Shortcuts\n\n### Long-Press Back Button\nFrom any nested view, long-press the back button to see the navigation stack. Tap any level to jump directly there, or hold to return to the project root.\n\n### Keyboard Shortcuts (Mac and iPad with keyboard)\n- **⌘N**: New file\n- **⌘F**: Find in file\n- **⌘G**: Find next\n- **⌘⇧G**: Find previous\n- **⌘B**: Bold\n- **⌘I**: Italic\n- **⌘U**: Underline\n\nSee [Keyboard Shortcuts](../09-reference/01-keyboard-shortcut-list.md) for the complete list.\n\n## Customizing the Interface\n\n### Appearance\nWriting Shed Pro follows your system's appearance settings:\n- Light mode\n- Dark mode\n- Automatic (follows system)\n\n### Text Size\nText in the editor respects your system's Dynamic Type settings. Increase system text size in Settings → Accessibility → Display & Text Size for larger editor text.\n\n## See Also\n- [The Editor](../04-writing/01-the-editor.md)\n- [Keyboard Shortcuts](../09-reference/01-keyboard-shortcut-list.md)\n- [Creating Your First Project](02-creating-your-first-project.md)\n\n---\n",
              "createdDate": "2026-02-03T08:09:41Z",
              "footnotes": [],
              "id": "5B844E00-F30C-475A-A54E-2FADE41AF4CE",
              "versionNumber": 1
