          "name": "103-page-setup",
          "sectionId": "1A4A60D7-55FE-49AF-9636-75122540D6B9",
          "userOrder": 2,
          "versions": [
            {
              "comments": [],
              "content": "# Page Setup\n\nPage Setup controls how your documents appear when exported or printed. Configure paper size, margins, headers, footers, and more.\n\n## Accessing Page Setup\n\n1. Open your project\n2. Go to **Project Settings**\n3. Select **Page Setup**\n\nPage setup applies to the entire project.\n\n## Paper Size\n\nChoose from standard paper sizes:\n\n| Size | Dimensions | Common Use |\n|------|------------|------------|\n| **Letter** | 8.5 × 11 inches | US standard |\n| **A4** | 210 × 297 mm | International standard |\n| **Legal** | 8.5 × 14 inches | US legal documents |\n| **A5** | 148 × 210 mm | Half of A4 |\n| **Custom** | Your dimensions | Special needs |\n\n### Choosing a Size\n- Match your printer's paper\n- Match submission requirements\n- Consider your audience's location (US uses Letter, most of world uses A4)\n\n## Orientation\n\n- **Portrait**: Taller than wide (default)\n- **Landscape**: Wider than tall\n\nMost writing uses portrait. Landscape might suit wide tables or special layouts.\n\n## Margins\n\nSet the space between page edge and content:\n\n### Margin Settings\n- **Top**: Space at page top\n- **Bottom**: Space at page bottom\n- **Left** (Inside): Left margin\n- **Right** (Outside): Right margin\n\n### Common Margin Sizes\n| Use Case | Margins |\n|----------|---------|\n| Standard manuscript | 1 inch all sides |\n| Printing with binding | 1.25\" left, 1\" others |\n| More content per page | 0.75\" all sides |\n\n### Considerations\n- Larger margins = more whitespace, easier reading\n- Smaller margins = more content per page\n- Some printers can't print to the edge\n\n## Headers and Footers\n\nAdd information at the top or bottom of every page:\n\n### Header Content\n- Author name\n- Document title\n- Custom text\n\n### Footer Content\n- Page numbers\n- Date\n- Custom text\n\n### Page Number Formats\n- Plain numbers (1, 2, 3)\n- With total (1 of 10)\n- Roman numerals (i, ii, iii)\n\n### Positioning\n- Left, Center, or Right aligned\n- First page can differ from others\n\n## First Page Different\n\nFor many documents:\n- First page has no header/footer (or different one)\n- Title page stands alone\n- Numbering starts on page 2\n\nToggle **First Page Different** to enable this.\n\n## Pagination View\n\nPreview your page setup:\n\n1. Open a file\n2. Switch to **Pagination View**\n3. See pages as they'll appear\n4. Verify margins, headers, footers\n5. Check page breaks\n\n## Page Setup for Different Uses\n\n### Standard Manuscript\n- Letter or A4 paper\n- 1-inch margins all around\n- Header: Name - Title - Page number\n- Double-spaced body text\n- First page: Title, author, word count\n\n### Poetry Collection\n- Comfortable margins (1-1.25 inches)\n- Page numbers in footer\n- Title at top of each poem page\n\n### Script\n- Industry-specific margins\n- Courier 12pt font\n- Specific header/footer format\n\n### Personal Reading\n- Whatever you prefer\n- Consider your reading environment\n\n## Page Breaks\n\nControl where pages break:\n\n### Automatic Breaks\nPages break naturally when content fills a page.\n\n### Manual Breaks\nInsert page breaks to force new pages:\n- Before chapters\n- After title pages\n- Where you need control\n\n### Widow/Orphan Control\nAvoid:\n- Single lines at page bottom (orphan)\n- Single lines at page top (widow)\nPagination engine handles this automatically.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Content Cut Off\n- Margins may be too small for printer\n- Check \"printable area\" of your printer\n- Increase margins slightly\n\n### Wrong Paper Size\n- Change in Page Setup\n- Ensure it matches printer settings\n\n### Headers/Footers Missing\n- Check they're enabled\n- Check \"First Page Different\" setting\n- Preview in Pagination View\n\n### Page Numbers Wrong\n- Check starting number setting\n- Check first page settings\n- Verify in Pagination View\n\n## See Also\n- [Export Options](../09-publishing/01-export-options.md)\n- [Printing](../09-publishing/04-printing.md)\n- [Stylesheet Editor](02-stylesheet-editor.md)\n\n---\n",
