              "comments": [],
              "content": "# Installation\n\nWriting Shed Pro is available on iPhone, iPad, and Mac through the App Store. This guide covers installation and initial setup.\n\n## System Requirements\n\n### iPhone and iPad\n- iOS 17.0 or later\n- iPadOS 17.0 or later\n- Works on all supported iPhone and iPad models\n\n### Mac\n- macOS 14.0 (Sonoma) or later\n- Mac Catalyst app (same app as iOS)\n- Works on Apple Silicon and Intel Macs\n\n## Installing from the App Store\n\n1. Open the **App Store** on your device\n2. Search for \"Writing Shed Pro\"\n3. Tap **Get** (or the price button)\n4. Authenticate with Face ID, Touch ID, or your Apple ID password\n5. Wait for the download to complete\n\nThe app icon appears on your Home Screen (iOS/iPadOS) or in Applications (Mac).\n\n## First Launch\n\nWhen you first open Writing Shed Pro:\n\n1. **iCloud Permission**: The app requests permission to use iCloud. We recommend enabling this for:\n   - Automatic backup of all your work\n   - Seamless sync between your devices\n   - No data loss if you lose or replace a device\n\n2. **Notifications**: Optional push notifications for submission reminders and deadlines\n\n3. **Empty Project List**: You'll see an empty project list, ready for you to create your first project\n\n## iCloud Setup\n\nWriting Shed Pro uses iCloud to store and sync your projects. To ensure this works:\n\n1. **Sign in to iCloud**: Settings → [Your Name] → iCloud\n2. **Enable iCloud Drive**: Settings → [Your Name] → iCloud → iCloud Drive: On\n3. **Enable Writing Shed Pro**: Settings → [Your Name] → iCloud → Apps Using iCloud → Writing Shed Pro: On\n\n### Without iCloud\n\nYou can use Writing Shed Pro without iCloud:\n- Projects are stored locally on your device\n- No sync between devices\n- Risk of data loss if device is lost or damaged\n- We strongly recommend enabling iCloud\n\n## Updating the App\n\nWriting Shed Pro updates automatically if you have automatic updates enabled. To update manually:\n\n1. Open the **App Store**\n2. Tap your profile icon in the top right\n3. Scroll down to see available updates\n4. Tap **Update** next to Writing Shed Pro\n\n## Reinstalling\n\nIf you delete and reinstall Writing Shed Pro:\n- With iCloud enabled: All your projects will sync back automatically\n- Without iCloud: Your local projects will be lost\n\n## Multiple Devices\n\nWriting Shed Pro works across all your Apple devices:\n\n1. Install on each device using the same Apple ID\n2. Ensure iCloud is enabled on all devices\n3. Your projects appear automatically on each device\n4. Changes sync within seconds\n\n### Sync Conflict Resolution\n\nIf you edit the same file on two devices simultaneously:\n- The most recent changes are preserved\n- Earlier changes are saved as a version\n- No data is ever lost\n\n## Troubleshooting Installation\n\n### App Won't Download\n- Check your internet connection\n- Ensure you have enough storage space\n- Try restarting the App Store (swipe up to close, reopen)\n- Restart your device\n\n### App Won't Open\n- Try force-quitting and reopening\n- Restart your device\n- Delete and reinstall the app (if iCloud is enabled, no data is lost)\n\n### iCloud Sync Not Working\nSee [iCloud Sync](04-icloud-sync.md) for detailed troubleshooting.\n\n## See Also\n- [Creating Your First Project](02-creating-your-first-project.md)\n- [iCloud Sync](04-icloud-sync.md)\n\n---\n",
              "createdDate": "2026-02-03T08:08:53Z",
