        {
          "contentTypeRaw": "markdown",
          "createdDate": "2026-02-03T15:15:06Z",
          "currentVersionIndex": 0,
          "id": "9F7ECD39-033B-41C9-ADF7-FEA86648B191",
          "includedInManuscript": true,
          "modifiedDate": "2026-02-03T15:18:14Z",
          "name": "95-submission-tracking",
          "sectionId": "95D841AA-7A8E-4DD8-99EE-874424C3609A",
          "userOrder": 4,
          "versions": [
            {
              "comments": [],
              "content": "# Submission Tracking\n\nWriting Shed Pro helps poets and fiction writers track where they've submitted their work. Know what's pending, accepted, or rejected at a glance.\n\n## Understanding Submissions\n\nThe submission system tracks:\n- **Publications**: Magazines, journals, competitions\n- **Submissions**: What you sent, when, and current status\n- **Submitted Files**: Which specific file versions you sent\n\n## Setting Up Publications\n\nBefore tracking submissions, define your target publications:\n\n### Creating a Publication\n1. Open the **Publications** folder\n2. Tap **+**\n3. Enter publication details:\n   - Name (e.g., \"Poetry Magazine\")\n   - Type (Magazine or Competition)\n   - URL (optional)\n   - Notes (optional)\n4. Tap **Create**\n\n### Publication Types\n- **Magazine**: Journals, literary magazines, online publications\n- **Competition**: Contests with deadlines and prizes\n\n### Organizing Publications\n- Create entries for places you submit to regularly\n- Add notes about guidelines, preferences, or past interactions\n- Update URLs if publications change\n\n## Creating Submissions\n\nWhen you send work out:\n\n### From a Collection\nThe recommended workflow:\n1. Create a Collection with the files to submit\n2. Open the Collection\n3. Tap **Submit to Publication**\n4. Select the publication\n5. Confirm submission details\n6. The submission is recorded\n\n### Direct Submission\n1. Open the **Submissions** folder\n2. Tap **+**\n3. Select the publication\n4. Choose files to include\n5. Set submission date\n6. Save\n\n### What Gets Recorded\n- Which files (and which versions)\n- Submission date\n- Target publication\n- Initial status (Pending)\n\n## Submission Statuses\n\nTrack the lifecycle of each submission:\n\n| Status | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| **Pending** | Submitted, awaiting response |\n| **Accepted** | Publication accepted the work |\n| **Rejected** | Publication declined |\n| **Withdrawn** | You withdrew the submission |\n\n### Updating Status\n1. Open the submission\n2. Change the status\n3. Add notes if desired (acceptance details, feedback)\n4. Save\n\n## Viewing Submissions\n\n### Submissions Folder\nAll submissions appear here:\n- Grouped by status\n- Shows publication name\n- Shows submission date\n- Shows file count\n\n### By Publication\nOpen a publication to see:\n- All submissions to that publication\n- History of your relationship\n- Acceptance rate\n\n### By File\nOpen a file's details to see:\n- Where it's been submitted\n- Current status of each submission\n- Submission history\n\n## Simultaneous Submissions\n\nMany writers submit the same work to multiple publications:\n1. Submit to Publication A\n2. Submit same file to Publication B\n3. Both submissions track independently\n4. When one accepts, update statuses appropriately\n\n### Managing Simultaneous Submissions\n- Check publication policies (some prohibit simultaneous submissions)\n- Keep track to avoid awkward situations\n- Withdraw from others promptly upon acceptance\n\n## Version Tracking\n\nSubmissions record the exact version you sent:\n- If you edit the file later, the submission still references the original version\n- You can see exactly what was submitted\n- Helpful if an editor references specific content\n\n## Workflow Tips\n\n### Before Submitting\n1. Move files to Ready folder\n2. Create a Collection for the submission package\n3. Proofread thoroughly\n4. Check submission guidelines\n\n### After Submitting\n1. Record the submission immediately\n2. Note any confirmation number\n3. Set a reminder notification for expected response time\n4. Monitor pending submissions\n\n## Notification Reminders\n\nWriting Shed Pro can send you notification reminders for submissions and publication deadlines.\n\n### Submission Reminders\nSet a reminder to follow up on a pending submission:\n1. Open the submission details\n2. Tap **Set Reminder**\n3. Choose a date and time\n4. A system notification will alert you when the reminder fires\n\n### Deadline Reminders\nSet a reminder for publication deadlines (magazines and competitions):\n1. Open the publication details\n2. Tap **Set Deadline Reminder**\n3. Choose a date and time\n4. You'll receive a notification before the deadline\n\n### Managing Reminders\n- Reminders appear as standard system notifications with alert and sound\n- You can cancel a reminder from the submission or publication detail view\n- The app will request notification permission the first time you set a reminder\n- Reminders are one-time notifications (they do not repeat)\n\n### Upon Response\n1. Update the status\n2. Add any feedback to notes\n3. If rejected, consider next submission target\n4. If accepted, celebrate!\n\n### Track Everything\n- Even quick online submissions\n- Even free publications\n- Build your submission history\n\n## Reports and Statistics\n\nView your submission activity:\n- Total submissions\n- Pending vs. completed\n- Acceptance rate\n- Response times\n\nUse this data to:\n- Identify responsive publications\n- See your progress\n- Plan future submissions\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Forgot to Record a Submission\n- Create it manually\n- Set the date to when you actually submitted\n- It's never too late to track\n\n### Status Changed Externally\n- Update in Writing Shed Pro to keep records accurate\n- Add notes explaining the situation\n\n### Files Changed After Submission\n- The submission still references the original version\n- You can see what was actually sent\n\n## See Also\n- [Collections](../10-advanced-features/104-collections.md)\n- [Organizing Your Work](../3-projects/35-organizing-your-work.md)\n- [Export Options](91-export-options.md)",
              "createdDate": "2026-02-03T15:15:06Z",
