          "name": "92-pdf-export",
          "sectionId": "95D841AA-7A8E-4DD8-99EE-874424C3609A",
          "userOrder": 1,
          "versions": [
            {
              "comments": [],
              "content": "# PDF Export\n\nPDF is the most reliable export format for sharing and submissions. The PDF looks identical on every device and platform.\n\n## Why PDF?\n\n### Advantages\n- **Universal**: Opens on any device\n- **Fixed**: Looks exactly as you designed it\n- **Secure**: Hard to accidentally edit\n- **Professional**: Industry standard for submissions\n\n### When to Use PDF\n- Submitting to magazines, agents, publishers\n- Sharing for review (where editing isn't needed)\n- Archiving finished work\n- Creating reading copies\n\n## Exporting to PDF\n\n### Single File\n1. Open the file you want to export\n2. Tap the **Share** or **Export** button\n3. Select **Export as PDF**\n4. Review settings if prompted\n5. Choose where to save or how to share\n\n### Multiple Files (Collection/Submission)\n1. Open the collection or submission\n2. Tap **Export**\n3. Select **PDF**\n4. Files combine into one PDF\n5. Save or share\n\n### Manuscript (Fiction)\n1. Assemble your manuscript\n2. Export as PDF\n3. All chapters included in order\n\n## PDF Settings\n\n### Page Setup\nBefore exporting, ensure your page setup is correct:\n- Paper size (Letter, A4, etc.)\n- Margins\n- Headers and footers\n- Orientation\n\nThese settings determine how the PDF appears.\n\n### Quality\n- Standard quality works for most uses\n- Higher quality for print-ready PDFs\n- Lower quality reduces file size\n\n### Page Range\n- All pages (default)\n- Specific pages if needed\n\n## What's Included in PDF\n\n### Always Included\n- All text with formatting\n- Paragraph styles\n- Images at current resolution\n- Footnotes in correct positions\n- Page numbers (if configured)\n- Headers/footers (if configured)\n\n### Hyperlinks\n- External links remain clickable\n- Internal links work within the PDF\n- Cross-file links point to correct pages\n\n### Not Included\n- Comments (by default)\n- Edit capability\n- Writer's notes\n\n## Previewing Before Export\n\nAlways preview before exporting:\n\n1. Switch to Pagination View\n2. Review each page\n3. Check:\n   - Page breaks\n   - Footnote placement\n   - Image positions\n   - Headers/footers\n4. Make adjustments if needed\n5. Then export\n\n## File Size Considerations\n\nPDF size depends on:\n- Number of pages\n- Number and size of images\n- Embedded fonts\n\n### Reducing File Size\n- Optimize images before inserting\n- Use fewer high-resolution images\n- Choose \"smaller file size\" option if available\n\n### When Size Matters\n- Email attachments (often limited to 25MB)\n- Some submission systems have limits\n- Cloud storage usage\n\n## Sharing PDFs\n\nAfter export, share via:\n- **Email**: Attach the PDF\n- **AirDrop**: Quick iOS/Mac sharing\n- **Cloud Storage**: Upload to iCloud, Dropbox, etc.\n- **Files App**: Save and access from other apps\n\n## PDF for Submissions\n\n### Standard Manuscript Requirements\nMany submissions expect:\n- Standard fonts (Times New Roman, Courier)\n- Double spacing\n- 1-inch margins\n- Page numbers\n- Author name/title in header\n\nConfigure these in Page Setup and Stylesheet before exporting.\n\n### Check Guidelines\nAlways read submission guidelines. Some specify:\n- Maximum file size\n- Specific formatting\n- Cover letter requirements\n- Naming conventions\n\n## Troubleshooting PDF Export\n\n### PDF Looks Different Than Expected\n- Check Pagination View first\n- Verify Page Setup settings\n- Ensure fonts are available\n\n### Images Missing or Wrong Size\n- Check original image quality\n- Verify image scale settings\n- Try re-inserting the image\n\n### PDF Too Large\n- Reduce image count/size\n- Choose smaller export quality\n- Compress after export if needed\n\n### Links Not Working\n- Ensure links were created correctly\n- Test in the exported PDF\n- Some PDF viewers handle links differently\n\n## See Also\n- [Export Options](01-export-options.md)\n- [Page Setup](../08-advanced-features/03-page-setup.md)\n- [Printing](04-printing.md)\n\n---\n",
              "createdDate": "2026-02-03T15:11:28Z",
