          "name": "53-file-organization",
          "sectionId": "3B0B704C-A12C-4AF7-B81F-8E8E0134AB98",
          "userOrder": 2,
          "versions": [
            {
              "comments": [],
              "content": "# File Organization in Prose Projects\n\nThis guide covers strategies for organizing files within Prose projects, from simple single-file documents to complex multi-file projects.\n\n## Organizing Strategies\n\n### Single-File Approach\nFor short documents (articles, essays, blog posts):\n- Create one file per document\n- Use workflow status to track progress\n- No sections needed\n\n### Multi-File Approach\nFor longer documents (user guides, book-length works):\n- Break content into logical files\n- Use sections to group related files\n- Order files within sections for export\n\n### Hybrid Approach\nMix both as needed:\n- Main content in organized sections\n- Supporting materials (notes, research) as standalone files\n\n## File Naming Conventions\n\nGood file names help you navigate your project quickly.\n\n### Recommended Patterns\n\n**Numbered Prefix**\n```\n01-introduction\n02-getting-started\n03-main-features\n04-advanced-topics\n```\n\n**Category Prefix**\n```\nguide-installation\nguide-features\nref-shortcuts\nref-faq\n```\n\n**Date Prefix (for journals/logs)**\n```\n2025-01-15-meeting-notes\n2025-01-20-project-update\n```\n\n### Naming Tips\n- Keep names concise but descriptive\n- Use lowercase with hyphens (avoids case-sensitivity issues)\n- Include numbers for ordering if sequence matters\n- Avoid special characters\n\n## Workflow Status Strategy\n\nUse workflow status to track where each file is in your process:\n\n### The Standard Flow\n```\nDraft → Ready → Published\n```\n\n1. **Draft**: Active writing/editing\n2. **Ready**: Complete, reviewed, ready for use\n3. **Published**: Final version, exported/published\n\n### Alternative Flows\n\n**For Ongoing Projects**\n```\nDraft → Ready (loop back as needed)\n```\n\n**For Review Process**\n```\nDraft → Ready (for review) → Published (after approval)\n```\n\n### Set Aside Status\nUse \"Set Aside\" for:\n- Content you might use later\n- Alternate versions\n- Archived material\n\nThis keeps your active lists focused.\n\n## Using Filters Effectively\n\n### Focus on Current Work\nFilter to **Draft** to see only work in progress.\n\n### Review Ready Files\nFilter to **Ready** when preparing to:\n- Export documents\n- Assign files to sections\n- Do final review\n\n### Check Published\nFilter to **Published** to see completed work.\n\n### View All\nSwitch to **All** for complete project overview.\n\n## Ordering Files\n\n### Manual Ordering (Within Sections)\nWhen viewing a section's files:\n1. Long-press a file to initiate drag\n2. Drop in the desired position\n3. Order is saved automatically\n\nThis order is used when exporting the section.\n\n### Alphabetical Ordering (Main List)\nIn the main Prose file list, files are sorted alphabetically by default. Use numbered prefixes in file names to control order.\n\n## The Trash Folder\n\nDeleted files go to Trash rather than being permanently removed.\n\n### Recovering Files\n1. Open the **Trash** folder\n2. Find the file\n3. Tap menu (⋯) → **Restore**\n4. File returns to the Prose folder\n\n### Permanent Deletion\n1. In Trash, tap **Edit**\n2. Select files\n3. Tap **Delete Forever**\n\n**Warning**: Permanent deletion cannot be undone.\n\n### Empty Trash\nTo delete all trashed files:\n1. Open Trash\n2. Tap **Empty Trash**\n3. Confirm\n\n## File Details\n\nView file information by tapping the menu (⋯) → **Details**:\n\n### Information Shown\n- **Created**: When the file was created\n- **Modified**: Last edit date/time\n- **Word Count**: Total words\n- **Character Count**: Total characters\n- **Section**: Which section (if any)\n- **Status**: Current workflow status\n\n## Import and Organization\n\nWhen importing files:\n1. Files are added to the Prose folder\n2. Status defaults to **Draft**\n3. Section is unassigned\n\n### Post-Import Steps\n1. Review imported content\n2. Rename if needed (menu → **Rename**)\n3. Change status when ready\n4. Assign to sections as appropriate\n\n## Export and Organization\n\nFile organization affects export:\n\n### Single File Export\nEach file exports as a separate document.\n\n### Section Export\nExport all files in a section as one combined document (in file order).\n\n### Project Export\nExport the entire project (all files) as one document.\n\n## Tips for Large Projects\n\n### Break Files by Topic\nOne topic per file is easier to manage than monolithic documents.\n\n### Use Sections for Major Divisions\nSections should represent major divisions (parts, chapters, categories).\n\n### Regular Cleanup\nPeriodically review:\n- Move completed work to Published\n- Set aside inactive files\n- Delete outdated content\n\n### Consistent Naming\nEstablish naming conventions early and stick to them.\n\n### Use Synopses\nAdd synopses to sections to remember what each contains.\n\n## See Also\n- [Prose Mode Overview](01-prose-mode-overview.md)\n- [Working with Sections](02-working-with-sections.md)\n- [Organizing Your Work](../03-projects/05-organizing-your-work.md)\n\n---\n",
              "createdDate": "2026-02-03T14:53:04Z",
              "footnotes": [],
              "id": "9E571CEE-9A9E-4E57-8012-EEFDDB19B2E1",
              "versionNumber": 1
            }
