          "name": "122-credits",
          "sectionId": "2103AD26-822D-4FD1-A157-653EF6E2FCFC",
          "versions": [
            {
              "comments": [],
              "content": "# Credits\n\nWriting Shed Pro was created with care for writers everywhere.\n\n## Development\n\nWriting Shed Pro is developed and maintained by its creator with a commitment to providing the best possible tools for creative writers.\n\n## Third-Party Resources\n\n### CMU Pronouncing Dictionary\nThe Carnegie Mellon University Pronouncing Dictionary powers our syllable counting and rhyme detection features.\n\n- **Source**: Carnegie Mellon University\n- **License**: BSD License\n- **Purpose**: Provides phonetic transcriptions for English words\n\n### Open Source Components\n\nWriting Shed Pro may incorporate open source software. Specific attributions and licenses are included in the app under Settings → Licenses.\n\n## Design Philosophy\n\nWriting Shed Pro was built on these principles:\n\n### Writers First\nEvery feature is designed with working writers in mind. Tools should support creativity, not interrupt it.\n\n### Cross-Platform Consistency\nWhether you're on iPhone, iPad, or Mac, Writing Shed Pro feels familiar and works the same way.\n\n### Your Words, Your Way\nFrom prose to poetry to drama, the app adapts to your writing style and project needs.\n\n### Privacy Respected\nYour writing is yours. We don't read it, analyze it, or share it.\n\n## Special Thanks\n\nGratitude to:\n- Beta testers who provided invaluable feedback\n- Writers who shared their workflow needs\n- The Swift and SwiftUI developer community\n- Everyone who reported bugs and suggested features\n\n## Feedback\n\nThe best features often come from user suggestions. If you have ideas for improving Writing Shed Pro, please share them through our support channels.\n\n## See Also\n- [Contact Support](../11-reference/05-contact-support.md)\n- [Legal](123-legal.md)\n\n---\n",
              "createdDate": "2026-02-09T12:47:11Z",
              "footnotes": [],
              "id": "7845EF42-2B9D-4954-959F-81866DE423F3",
              "versionNumber": 1
            }
          ],
          "workflowStatus": "ready"
        },
        {
          "contentTypeRaw": "markdown",
          "createdDate": "2026-02-09T12:47:29Z",
          "currentVersionIndex": 0,
          "id": "6B4894B9-8CEC-4A0E-B706-968930822C2D",
          "includedInManuscript": true,
          "modifiedDate": "2026-02-09T12:51:38Z",
          "name": "123-legal",
          "sectionId": "2103AD26-822D-4FD1-A157-653EF6E2FCFC",
          "versions": [
            {
              "comments": [],
              "content": "# Legal\n\n## Copyright\n\nCopyright © 2025–2026 Keith Pro Apps. All rights reserved.\n\nWriting Shed Pro and the Writing Shed Pro logo are trademarks of Keith Pro Apps.\n\n## License Agreement\n\nWriting Shed Pro is licensed, not sold, to you by Keith Pro Apps for use under the terms of the Apple Licensed Application End User License Agreement (EULA), available at [https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/](https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/).\n\n## Privacy\n\nWriting Shed Pro does not collect, store, or transmit any personal data. All your writing remains on your device and in your personal iCloud account (if enabled). No analytics, tracking, or telemetry data is gathered.\n\nFor full details, see our Privacy Policy at [writingshed.com/privacy](https://writingshed.com/privacy).\n\n## Third-Party Components\n\n### CMU Pronouncing Dictionary\n\nThe syllable counting and rhyme tools use the CMU Pronouncing Dictionary, provided by Carnegie Mellon University. Used under the terms of the CMU Pronouncing Dictionary license.\n\n### Apple Frameworks\n\nWriting Shed Pro is built using Apple's SwiftUI, SwiftData, CloudKit, and other Apple frameworks, subject to Apple's terms and conditions.\n\n## Disclaimer\n\nWriting Shed Pro is provided \"as is\" without warranty of any kind. While every effort is made to ensure reliability and data integrity, the developer is not liable for any loss of data or content. Users are encouraged to maintain regular backups of their work through iCloud or manual export.\n\n## Contact\n\nFor legal enquiries, contact [legal@writingshed.com](mailto:legal@writingshed.com).\n\n## See Also\n- [Contact Support](../11-reference/115-contact-support.md)\n- [Credits](122-credits.md)",
